                <pb facs="0975" n="967" sameAs="frus:frus1938v01/pg967"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">540.61B3/262: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in
                        Switzerland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Keith</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-09-07T19:00:00-04:00">September 7, 1938—7
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>44. Your despatch no. 497, August 18, 1938.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d932-f1"/>
                    Please inform the Secretary General of the League of Nations that the President
                    has approved the designation of Mr. Curtis T. Everett, American Consul at
                    Geneva, as the delegate of the United States to the conference in regard to the
                    moving picture films convention. Everett is also being informed to this
                    effect.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
